### Summary

In `distribution_database.rs`, `get_wheel` handles streaming failures differently depending on the source.

For `BuiltDist::Registry` (line ~240), the match catches `Error::Extract` and falls back to downloading the full wheel when streaming fails or is unsupported:

```rust
Err(Error::Extract(name, err)) => {
    if err.is_http_streaming_unsupported() {
        // fall back to download_wheel
    } else if err.is_http_streaming_failed() {
        // fall back to download_wheel
    } else {
        return Err(Error::Extract(name, err));
    }
    // ...download_wheel...
}
```

For `BuiltDist::DirectUrl` (line ~317), the match only catches `Error::Client` with `is_http_streaming_unsupported()`:

```rust
Err(Error::Client(err)) if err.is_http_streaming_unsupported() => {
    // fall back to download_wheel
}
```

So if streaming extraction fails (not just unsupported) for a direct URL wheel, uv errors out instead of falling back to a full download. The registry path recovers from both cases.

Related: #5073, #17847 (streaming/download fallback area).

