### Summary

Adding an option `workspace_dir` to tool.uv.sources, so another workspace can be searched for dependencies.

### Example

#### Current behavior

When I have a workspaces, it is easy to look for packages in the workspace
```
[tool.uv.sources]
package_a-x = { workspace = true }
package_a-y = { workspace = true }
``` 

But, if I have a second workspace, I have to link all the dependencies from that workspace per path:
```
[tool.uv.sources]
package_a-x = { workspace = true }
package_a-y = { workspace = true }
package_b-x = { path = "../package_b/x", editable = true }
package_b-y = { path = "../package_b/y", editable = true }
```

#### Feature behavior

Would it be possible to add an option e.g. `workspace_dir` , where the other workspace is searched for that package? So:
```
[tool.uv.sources]
package_a-x = { workspace = true }
package_a-y = { workspace = true }
package_b-x = { workspace_dir = "../package_b"}
package_b-y = { workspace_dir = "../package_b"}
```
